virglrenderer: test hook to refuse marked shaders (test runtimes only)

What: OMACVM_VIRGL_TEST_FAIL_GLSL=<text> makes vrend treat every shader whose
GLSL contains <text> as refused by the host compiler. tests/graphics uses the
bits of the float 4242.25 (1166316032; Mesa sends immediates as UINT32) so one
WebGL shader of the test page fails on purpose.
Why: a real host compile failure that the guest's Mesa lets through is a bug we
fix when we find it; the robustness paths need a failure on demand.
Applied only when build-qemu-gpu-runtime.sh runs with OMACVM_RUNTIME_TEST_HOOKS=1;
release runtimes never contain it.
Upstream: not applicable.
Tests: tests/graphics/context-loss.sh, tests/graphics/guest/gl-lost.c.
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -1512,6 +1512,13 @@
       }
    }
 
+   /* Test builds only: refuse shaders whose GLSL contains this text, like the host GL
+    * refusing a shader the guest compiled (tests/graphics/context-loss.sh). */
+   const char *fail_marker = getenv("OMACVM_VIRGL_TEST_FAIL_GLSL");
+   bool inject_failure = false;
+   for (int i = 0; fail_marker && *fail_marker && i < shader->glsl_strings.num_strings; i++)
+      inject_failure |= strstr(shader_parts[i], fail_marker) != NULL;
+
    shader->id = glCreateShader(conv_shader_type(shader->sel->type));
    glShaderSource(shader->id, shader->glsl_strings.num_strings, shader_parts, NULL);
    glCompileShader(shader->id);
@@ -1523,6 +1530,10 @@
    }
 
    glGetShaderiv(shader->id, GL_COMPILE_STATUS, &param);
+   if (inject_failure) {
+      virgl_error("OMACVM_VIRGL_TEST_FAIL_GLSL: refusing a shader on purpose\n");
+      param = GL_FALSE;
+   }
    if (param == GL_FALSE) {
